nr_{\\alpha(j)\\alpha(j')} \\circ \\varphi_j \\times \\varphi_{j'}).\n$$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{T}$", "MATH_0032": "$\\mathcal{T}'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-quotient-stack}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0008": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:287e8047d97d4e3bd3628c61d5a51800e41a4f05ba1f8539b0f12a066218f3f5", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:30ce603d48fa85a82c02c8fa7620740e6e5092be12aca5c35a384c11502420c8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e0d4e6bd9a29d00789c6a8846c342c1fbd198ec29900524fd56345f6d9b73ca8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn order to formulate the result we need to introduce some\nnotation. Assume <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are as in\nDefinition <REF_0001> (1).\nLet <MATH_0003> be a scheme over <MATH_0004>. Let <MATH_0005>\nbe an fppf covering. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0006>-descent datum<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> relative\nto <MATH_0007> is given by a system <MATH_0008> where\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> for each <MATH_0009> a morphism <MATH_0010>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> for each <MATH_0011> a morphism <MATH_0012>\n<STRUCT_0005>\nsuch that\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(a)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> as morphisms <MATH_0013> we have\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(b)<ITEMCLOSE_0002> as morphisms <MATH_0014> we have\n<MATH_0015>\n<STRUCT_0007>\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism <MATH_0016> between two\n<MATH_0017>-descent data<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> over the same covering <MATH_0018>\nis a collection <MATH_0019> such that\n<STRUCT_0008>\n<ITEMOPEN_0003><ITEMCLOSE_0003> <MATH_0020> as morphisms <MATH_0021> we have\n<MATHSEG_0003>and<MATHSEG_0004>\n<ITEMOPEN_0004><ITEMCLOSE_0004> <MATH_0022> as morphisms <MATH_0023> we have\n<MATH_0024>\n<STRUCT_0009>\nThere is a natural composition law on morphisms of descent data relative\nto a fixed covering and we obtain a category of descent data.\nThis category is a groupoid. Finally, if\n<MATH_0025>\nis a second fppf covering which refines <MATH_0026> then there\nis a notion of pullback of descent data. This is particularly easy to\ndescribe explicitly in this case. Namely, if <MATH_0027> and\n<MATH_0028> is the morphism of coverings, then\nthe pullback of the descent datum <MATH_0029> is simply\n<MATH_0030>\nPullback defined in this manner defines a functor from the category of\ndescent data over <MATH_0031> to the category of descend data over\n<MATH_0032>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:365030c3a3e33ec57caa7fcf35b7889054cbb82556cad6ed26f7bc35957ad018", "unit_id": "tag:04MB:prose-0001"}
